<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50566" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vermĭcŭlus</span></b> , i,
			m.
		dim.
		vermis, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a little worm</i>, <i>grub</i>, in
			decaying things. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i><span class="en">Lucr. 2,
			899</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 10, 65, 85, § 186</span></i>:  in linguā canum, <i><span class="en">id. 29, 5,
				32, § 100</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A disease of dogs which drives them mad</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Grat. Cyn.
			386</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			In the Vulgate, <i>the scarlet worm</i>, for coccum
				(<i>scarlet color</i>), <i><span class="en">Vulg. Exod.
				35, 25</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">Hier. Ep. 64,
			19</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">VERMICVLVM STRAVERVNT,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 4240</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Inscr. Murat. p. 114,
		2</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
